  <h1>About salarynegotiationcalc.com</h1>
  <p>salarynegotiationcalc.com is a free compensation strategy resource maintained by The Click Lab. Our calculator and editorial guides help job seekers and professionals understand their market value, estimate appropriate negotiation targets, and navigate salary conversations with confidence.</p>

  <h2>What This Site Is</h2>
  <p>Most professionals leave significant money on the table in salary negotiations — either by not negotiating at all (studies consistently show 40–60% of job seekers fail to negotiate even when they receive an offer) or by anchoring too close to an offer without the research to justify a higher ask. The gap between the compensation most people accept and what they could achieve with effective negotiation compounds dramatically over a career. A $5,000 difference in starting salary, growing with each subsequent negotiation and merit increase, represents hundreds of thousands of dollars in lifetime earnings.</p>
  <p>This site exists to reduce that gap. The calculator models the labor market variables that drive salary — industry, location, experience — and produces a concrete negotiation target range and opening anchor number that is grounded in published data. The guides explain the negotiation process, the research methodology, and the psychological dynamics that determine who gets more and why.</p>

  <h2>What We Cover</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The calculator:</strong> A salary range estimation tool applying BLS and commercial salary database industry multipliers, geographic location premiums, and experience adjustments to produce market rate estimates and negotiation targets.</li>
    <li><strong>Negotiation types:</strong> New job offer negotiation, annual review strategy, promotion negotiation, equity and total compensation analysis, and counter-offer evaluation.</li>
    <li><strong>Research methodology:</strong> How to use Glassdoor, Levels.fyi, LinkedIn Salary, and peer network data to build a defensible salary ask.</li>
    <li><strong>Tactical guidance:</strong> Anchoring, timing, handling "non-negotiable" pushback, structuring a counter-offer, and managing multiple competing offers.</li>
    <li><strong>Total compensation:</strong> Beyond base salary — signing bonuses, equity, benefits, remote flexibility, and other components that determine the true value of a compensation package.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What We Don't Do</h2>
  <p>We do not provide personalized career advice or compensation consulting. The calculator produces estimates based on published labor market data; actual compensation for any specific role depends on many factors the calculator cannot model, including the specific company&rsquo;s pay bands, the candidate&rsquo;s specific skill set and track record, and the state of the labor market for the specific role at the time of the negotiation. We do not accept sponsored content or referral arrangements with employers or recruiters.</p>

